/// A [Message] transformer for the PERSISTENCE path (session JSONL):
/// masks secrets inside AssistantMessage tool-call arguments.
///
/// gh-1952 review: the redaction hooks mask content blocks and tool
/// RESULTS, never `toolCalls[].arguments` — so a registered secret a
/// command embeds (the #1408 approvedSecretLiterals hatch explicitly
/// allows authored commands to carry it) persisted RAW into the
/// "persisted, shareable record". Execution is unaffected: this runs on
/// the record-write path only, after the live arguments already reached
/// `env.exec` byte-identically (I1); the provider context keeps the raw
/// arguments too (shaping it would change what the model sees —
/// `transformContext` must NOT mask call arguments).
///
/// Write-side-exempt tools (`redactionExemptTools`, issue #24 AC7) are
/// skipped: their arguments are the model-authored deliverable, and the
/// persisted record must match the bytes actually written.
Message persistRedactMessage(RedactionPipeline pipeline, Message message) {
 if (message is! AssistantMessage) return message;
 var changed = false;
